    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "In 261 BCE, the tragic Kalinga War transformed Emperor Ashoka, leading him to embrace Buddhism and propagate Dhamma.",
        "In 1568 CE, with the fall of King Mukundadeva, Odisha lost its independence to the Bengal Sultanate.",
        "The Paika Rebellion of 1817, led by Bakshi Jagabandhu in Khordha, was a major early armed uprising against British rule.",
        "On April 1, 1936, Odisha became the first British Indian state formed on a linguistic basis, commemorated as Utkal Divas.",
        "In 1948, the capital of Odisha was officially shifted from Cuttack to Bhubaneswar."
      ],
